1
00:00:00,860 --> 00:00:04,980
OpenChronology is one editor
that runs in several places:

2
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:08,370
on the website, in your
browser without an account,

3
00:00:08,420 --> 00:00:14,250
as a desktop app, and as a single
offline file. It works the same in each.

4
00:00:14,300 --> 00:00:17,991
What changes is where
your timeline is kept.

5
00:00:19,451 --> 00:00:24,761
On the website, at timescale.info
or any OpenChronology server,

6
00:00:24,811 --> 00:00:28,001
you sign in and save
timelines to your account.

7
00:00:28,051 --> 00:00:31,421
Each one starts private. From
there you can share a link,

8
00:00:31,471 --> 00:00:37,581
embed it on a page, add collaborators,
and every save is kept in its history.

9
00:00:37,631 --> 00:00:40,931
One honest note: private means
hidden from other users,

10
00:00:40,981 --> 00:00:44,398
not hidden from the people
who run that server.

11
00:00:45,858 --> 00:00:50,108
Without an account, you can still
start a timeline in the browser.

12
00:00:50,158 --> 00:00:55,588
It lives only in that tab, so export
it as a file before you close it.

13
00:00:55,638 --> 00:01:00,865
Signed in, your browser keeps drafts for
you until you save them to the server.

14
00:01:02,335 --> 00:01:06,735
The desktop app, for
Windows, macOS and Linux,

15
00:01:06,785 --> 00:01:12,685
keeps timelines as files on your own
computer, and works with no network at all.

16
00:01:12,735 --> 00:01:17,445
Large timelines stay quick, because
it reads only what's on screen.

17
00:01:17,495 --> 00:01:21,065
When you want to share,
connect it to timescale.info,

18
00:01:21,115 --> 00:01:24,553
or to your own server,
or to several at once.

19
00:01:26,043 --> 00:01:30,663
And the offline file is the
whole editor in one HTML file.

20
00:01:30,713 --> 00:01:35,533
It never uses the network, so you can
carry it on a stick or open it on a

21
00:01:35,583 --> 00:01:39,743
machine that's never online.
Nothing is kept when you close it,

22
00:01:39,793 --> 00:01:41,751
so export your work.

23
00:01:43,221 --> 00:01:48,831
An .ochx file opens in every one of
them, with its display settings,

24
00:01:48,881 --> 00:01:53,581
its plugins and copies of its
pictures. So start offline,

25
00:01:53,631 --> 00:01:57,471
finish on the website, or
move to a server of your own:

26
00:01:57,521 --> 00:02:00,956
the free server packages
run the same platform.

27
00:02:02,406 --> 00:02:08,076
To share, use the website. To keep
it yours, use the desktop app.

28
00:02:08,126 --> 00:02:12,056
To stay offline, use the
file. They're all free,

29
00:02:12,106 --> 00:02:13,860
under Download.
